# Latency & Redundancy Analysis — ConvergentAI Codebase

Full audit of backend agent pipeline, context management, prompt system, frontend connection flow, and API surface for issues that increase latency or create redundancy.

---

## 🔴 Critical — Direct Latency Impact

### 1. Serial LLM Extraction Calls in `runStage3BExtraction` (Biggest Offender)

**File:** [session-context-manager.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/context/session-context-manager.ts#L252-L284)

The `employment_details` field fires **3 sequential LLM calls** — `extractProfileField()` for title, years, and self-employed status — each a full Groq API round-trip (~200-400ms each). Same pattern in `declarations` (2 sequential calls).

```typescript
// Lines 253-276: Three serial awaits = ~600-1200ms stacked latency
const resTitle = await extractProfileField(text, lastQuestion, 'employment_position', ...);
const resYears = await extractProfileField(text, lastQuestion, 'employment_years', ...);
const resSelf  = await extractProfileField(text, lastQuestion, 'self_employed', ...);
```

> [!CAUTION]
> This adds **600-1200ms of pure network latency** to every user turn during employment data collection. These calls are independent and can be parallelized with `Promise.all()`.

**Fix:** Wrap all independent extractions in `Promise.all()`:
```typescript
const [resTitle, resYears, resSelf] = await Promise.all([
  extractProfileField(text, lastQuestion, 'employment_position', ...),
  extractProfileField(text, lastQuestion, 'employment_years', ...),
  extractProfileField(text, lastQuestion, 'self_employed', ...),
]);
```

Similarly in [lines 300-315](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/context/session-context-manager.ts#L300-L315) — `declarations` has 2 serial calls that should be parallelized.

