### 2. Duplicate LLM Instance Creation — `summarizationLlm` vs `createVadAgent` LLM

**File:** [agent.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/agent.ts#L82-L118)

Two separate `openai.LLM` instances are created for the same Groq endpoint + model, with identical configuration:

```typescript
// Line 82-86: Summarization LLM
const summarizationLlm = new openai.LLM({
  model: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile',
  baseURL: 'https://api.groq.com/openai/v1',
  apiKey: getDynamicGroqApiKey() || ailanaConfig.groqApiKey,
});

// Line 114-118: Agent LLM (inside createVadAgent, called multiple times on rotation)
llm: new openai.LLM({
  model: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile',
  baseURL: 'https://api.groq.com/openai/v1',
  apiKey: getDynamicGroqApiKey() || ailanaConfig.groqApiKey,
}),
```

> [!WARNING]
> Every session rotation creates yet another `openai.LLM` instance. These share no connection pool or caching. The `summarizationLlm` could be reused as the agent's LLM (they hit the same API with the same model).

