### 3. `getDynamicGroqApiKey()` Logs on Every Call — Console I/O in Hot Path

**File:** [ailana-config.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/config/ailana-config.ts#L35-L43)

```typescript
export function getDynamicGroqApiKey(): string {
  const raw = process.env.GROQ_API_KEY ?? '';
  const keys = raw.split(',').map(k => k.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  // ...
  console.log(`[config]: Selected rotated Groq API key ending in: ...${selectedKey.slice(-4)}`);
  return selectedKey;
}
```

This function is called:
- In `createVadAgent()` (every rotation)
- In `generateTextOnlyReply()` (every text message)
- In `extractProfileField()` (every extraction — up to 3x per turn)
- In `classifyConfirmation()` (every confirmation)

> [!WARNING]
> The `console.log` fires on **every single LLM call** in the system. On a busy turn with 3 parallel extractions + the main LLM, that's 4+ log lines of sync I/O. The `process.env` parse + split + map + filter chain also re-runs every time — this should be cached.

**Fix:** Cache the parsed key array at module load, rotate via a pre-built array. Remove or gate the log behind a debug flag.

