### 4. `openaiClient.apiKey` Mutation Before Every LLM Call

**File:** [llm-extractor.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/context/llm-extractor.ts#L4-L7)

```typescript
// Module-level singleton
const openaiClient = new OpenAI({
  apiKey: ailanaConfig.groqApiKey,  // Captures the key at import time
  baseURL: 'https://api.groq.com/openai/v1',
});
```

Then on [line 43](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/context/llm-extractor.ts#L43) and [line 99](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/context/llm-extractor.ts#L99):
```typescript
openaiClient.apiKey = getDynamicGroqApiKey() || ailanaConfig.groqApiKey;
```

> [!WARNING]
> **Race condition + redundancy.** Mutating a shared singleton's `apiKey` before every call means concurrent extraction calls could overwrite each other's key mid-flight. This is both a correctness risk and adds overhead from the `getDynamicGroqApiKey()` + `console.log` on every invocation. If parallelizing the extractions (fix #1), this becomes an **active race condition**.

**Fix:** Pass the API key into each call, or create a short-lived client per call, or resolve the key once at the start of `onUserTurn()` and thread it through.

