### 5. `updateSessionInstructions` Redundantly Runs Twice Per Voice Turn

**File:** [agent.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/agent.ts#L29-L59) and [lines 289-319](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/agent.ts#L289-L319)

In `onUserTurnCompleted`:
```typescript
// Line 36: Calls updateSessionInstructions() via the closure
this.updateInstructions();

// Lines 39-58: Then ALSO manually patches the local chatCtx
const activeInstructions = this.contextManager.getActiveInstructions();
const systemItem = chatCtx.items.find(...);
if (systemItem) {
  systemItem.content = [activeInstructions];
  ...
```

The `updateInstructions` function (line 289-319) **does the exact same work** — finds the system item, updates content, patches the ID. The hook then immediately does it again on the local chatCtx copy.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `getActiveInstructions()` calls `buildSessionPrompt()` which concatenates Layer 1 + Layer 2 + Layer 3 — a non-trivial string assembly with template interpolation. This runs **twice** per turn.

