### 6. Emotion Polling via `setInterval(500ms)` Scans Entire Chat History

**File:** [agent.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/agent.ts#L191-L215)

```typescript
emotionEvalInterval = setInterval(() => {
  const items = session.chatCtx?.items || [];
  const lastAssistantItem = items.slice().reverse().find(
    (i) => i.type === 'message' && i.role === 'assistant'
  );
  if (lastAssistantItem?.textContent) {
    const emotion = evaluateEmotion(lastAssistantItem.textContent);
    // ...publishes data channel message
  }
}, 500);
```

> [!NOTE]
> Every 500ms during speaking:
> 1. Copies the entire items array (`.slice()`)
> 2. Reverses it
> 3. Searches for the last assistant message
> 4. Runs regex evaluation
> 5. Encodes + publishes a DataChannel message (even when emotion hasn't changed — though there's a guard for that)
>
> The `items.slice().reverse()` is O(n) array copy + reverse on every tick. With long conversations, this becomes measurably wasteful. Use `findLast()` or iterate from the end with a simple for-loop.

