## 🟡 Moderate — Redundancy & Inefficiency

### 8. `prepareContext()` Calls Both `maybeCompact()` AND `maybeRotate()` Sequentially

**File:** [agent.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/agent.ts#L154-L164)

```typescript
const prepareContext = async () => {
  // ...filters handoff items
  await contextManager.maybeCompact(session, vadAgent, isIdle);
  await contextManager.maybeRotate(session, createAgentForRotation, isIdle);
};
```

Both `maybeCompact` and `maybeRotate` call `chatCtx._summarize()` — a full LLM summarization call. If both triggers fire on the same turn, you get **two back-to-back summarization calls**, the second of which re-summarizes an already-summarized context.

In [session-context-manager.ts](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/backend/src/context/session-context-manager.ts#L980-L1008), `rotate()` also calls `_summarize()`:
```typescript
const summarized = await chatCtx._summarize(this.summarizationLlm, {
  keepLastTurns: 2,
});
```

> [!WARNING]
> A single idle transition can trigger compact (which summarizes) and then rotate (which summarizes again). The rotate should check if compact already ran and skip re-summarization.

