### 14. `agentMediaStream` Recalculated on Every Render (Not Memoized)

**File:** [keyframe-avatar.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/src/components/keyframe-avatar.tsx#L71-L88)

```typescript
const agentMediaStream: MediaStream | undefined = (() => {
  let agent = participants.find((p) => p.identity === "agent" || p.identity.startsWith("agent-"));
  if (!agent) agent = participants.find((p) => !p.identity.startsWith("guest_"));
  // ...
})();
```

This IIFE runs on **every render** — not wrapped in `useMemo`. Since `useParticipants()` triggers re-renders on any participant change (joins, leaves, track updates), this search runs frequently. The `useEffect` on [line 392-397](file:///c:/Users/Sameer/Desktop/ConvergentAI/src/components/keyframe-avatar.tsx#L392-L397) depends on `agentMediaStream`, causing the audio pipe to tear down and rebuild if the reference changes (which it does on every render since it's a new object each time).

> [!WARNING]
> Without memoization, the audio pipe (AudioContext + AudioWorklet) is **torn down and rebuilt** on every participant event. This causes audible audio glitches and unnecessary latency.

